    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d136-a9">

                <pb facs="0324" n="234" sameAs="frus:frus1875v01/pg234"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 9 in No. 11.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Address read at the audience.</hi></head>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sire</hi>: I was charged by the President, on
                    receiving his appointment to reside near you as minister for the United States,
                    to present to your Imperial Majesty his salutations, and to express his renewed
                    assurance of the friendship entertained for China. He hopes that your reign may
                    be happy and long continued, and marked by constant advancement and prosperity
                    in everything that will benefit this land and people.</p>
                <p>He is pleased to know that more than sixty thousand of your Imperial Majesty’s
                    subjects, who are now in the United States, are actively engaged in every
                    industrial pursuit and science; and this fact gives my country a closer interest
                    in this than any other can feel, and still more strengthens the bonds which have
                    always existed to bring our two nations into amicable relations.</p>
                <p>I have now the honor, sire, to lay before you the letter which accredits me as
                    envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary at the court of your Imperial
                    Majesty.</p>
            </div>
